1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:02,700
(EP04 Behind-the-Scenes)

2
00:00:02,740 --> 00:00:05,980
(Behind-the-Scenes 1)

3
00:00:06,020 --> 00:00:07,980
(The Night Before the Stargazing Room Date)

4
00:00:12,660 --> 00:00:13,380
(Rummaging)

5
00:00:13,420 --> 00:00:14,340
(Rummaging)

6
00:00:30,060 --> 00:00:31,740
(Laughing at Herself)
This is way too obvious.

7
00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:33,940
Forget it.

8
00:00:42,420 --> 00:00:43,700
(Observing)

9
00:00:45,310 --> 00:00:46,110
Run!

10
00:00:58,190 --> 00:00:59,830
Does this light up too?

11
00:01:00,510 --> 00:01:01,420
It can light up

12
00:01:01,420 --> 00:01:03,070
and play music.

13
00:01:03,350 --> 00:01:04,710
Is it a music box?

14
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:06,620
Yeah, a music box.

15
00:01:07,140 --> 00:01:07,700
Okay.

16
00:01:08,110 --> 00:01:10,100
Then you can give it to him
when you go to the stargazing room.

17
00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:10,540
Yeah.

18
00:01:12,460 --> 00:01:17,420
(Behind-the-Scenes 2)

19
00:01:17,460 --> 00:01:22,060
(Behind-the-Scenes)

20
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:22,820
This music

21
00:01:22,820 --> 00:01:25,030
really sounds like rain.

22
00:01:25,710 --> 00:01:27,340
Do you like rainy days?

23
00:01:27,340 --> 00:01:28,750
I actually quite like them.

24
00:01:29,430 --> 00:01:31,750
But the downside is you can't go out
and have fun.

25
00:01:33,430 --> 00:01:35,190
Sounds like you'd rather go out.

26
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:37,620
Since I spend a lot of time
at home anyway.

27
00:01:38,230 --> 00:01:39,380
When it's raining outside,

28
00:01:39,380 --> 00:01:39,980
it just

29
00:01:39,980 --> 00:01:41,150
feels really cozy.

30
00:01:41,260 --> 00:01:42,300
(Agrees)

31
00:01:42,300 --> 00:01:43,390
So really,

32
00:01:43,910 --> 00:01:45,670
you just like the sound of rain.

33
00:01:46,980 --> 00:01:47,740
Yeah.

34
00:01:49,780 --> 00:01:51,380
(Glances)

35
00:01:52,590 --> 00:01:54,070
I wonder
what time we'll be back tomorrow.

36
00:01:54,070 --> 00:01:55,870
I feel like we might hit traffic
on the way back.

37
00:01:56,230 --> 00:01:56,950
It's okay.

38
00:01:56,950 --> 00:01:58,910
I'll pick you up tomorrow.

39
00:01:59,350 --> 00:02:01,150
But I'm worried about traffic.

40
00:02:01,710 --> 00:02:02,630
It's fine.

41
00:02:04,070 --> 00:02:05,660
If so, we'd just get
to spend more time together.

42
00:02:05,660 --> 00:02:06,460
Yeah.

43
00:02:13,540 --> 00:02:15,740
(Smiles)

44
00:02:17,940 --> 00:02:22,900
(Behind-the-Scenes 3)

45
00:02:23,310 --> 00:02:24,630
(Behind-the-Scenes)
Come play a round with us.

46
00:02:24,630 --> 00:02:25,820
Loser does ten squats.

47
00:02:25,820 --> 00:02:27,580
I don't even know how to play pool.

48
00:02:27,580 --> 00:02:28,590
Then I'll let you win.

49
00:02:29,190 --> 00:02:30,790
I feel like I won't sink a single ball.

50
00:02:30,790 --> 00:02:31,260
Just give it a try.

51
00:02:31,260 --> 00:02:32,660
Hit it straight.

52
00:02:32,660 --> 00:02:34,870
Like this. Hit this one

53
00:02:34,870 --> 00:02:35,790
and knock it into the pocket.

54
00:02:36,110 --> 00:02:36,740
Try it like this.

55
00:02:36,740 --> 00:02:37,620
Just hit it straight.

56
00:02:37,860 --> 00:02:38,500
Sorry.

57
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:40,030
Was that an attack on your opponent?

58
00:02:40,030 --> 00:02:41,100
(Accepting Punishment)

59
00:02:42,260 --> 00:02:44,310
When you're hitting straight,
stand a little closer.

60
00:02:46,580 --> 00:02:47,390
Like this?

61
00:02:48,870 --> 00:02:50,550
There's actually quite a lot
to the technique,

62
00:02:50,550 --> 00:02:51,150
I think.

63
00:02:51,150 --> 00:02:52,220
(Laughs)

64
00:02:53,470 --> 00:02:54,380
This pose is pretty elegant.

65
00:02:54,380 --> 00:02:54,900
Really?

66
00:02:55,100 --> 00:02:55,900
(Imitates)
Like this?

67
00:02:57,190 --> 00:02:58,780
Why don't you show me?

68
00:02:58,870 --> 00:02:59,830
Basically, your feet...

69
00:02:59,830 --> 00:03:00,630
Look, for example,

70
00:03:00,870 --> 00:03:01,950
one of your feet...

71
00:03:01,950 --> 00:03:03,220
Say the cue ball is here.

72
00:03:03,350 --> 00:03:04,310
(Tutorial Begins)
Your foot should line up

73
00:03:04,310 --> 00:03:05,550
with it.

74
00:03:05,550 --> 00:03:06,830
Like, imagine a straight line.

75
00:03:07,230 --> 00:03:07,910
This foot points forward.

76
00:03:07,910 --> 00:03:08,590
Just keep it natural.

77
00:03:08,590 --> 00:03:10,030
Then lower your body,

78
00:03:10,030 --> 00:03:11,430
and keep your chin close to the cue.

79
00:03:11,870 --> 00:03:13,510
That way, you'll aim straight.

80
00:03:15,540 --> 00:03:16,100
Look.

81
00:03:16,100 --> 00:03:17,470
You're not listening
to a single word I'm saying.

82
00:03:18,110 --> 00:03:18,900
I mean...

83
00:03:18,900 --> 00:03:19,700
This is so annoying.

84
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:21,790
I'll just poke it in
and be done with it.

85
00:03:22,100 --> 00:03:23,630
Let me try poking it.

86
00:03:26,860 --> 00:03:27,620
Yeah.

87
00:03:30,590 --> 00:03:32,870
Badminton suits me better.

88
00:03:33,310 --> 00:03:34,790
Let's go. We can play badminton instead.

89
00:03:34,790 --> 00:03:35,580
Okay.

90
00:03:36,900 --> 00:03:41,860
(Behind-the-Scenes 4)

91
00:03:41,900 --> 00:03:42,900
(Behind-the-Scenes)

92
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:43,540
(Wu Xingying & Sun Bohan's city date)

93
00:03:43,540 --> 00:03:44,300
Xing,

94
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:47,070
do you like your current job?

95
00:03:47,630 --> 00:03:48,830
It's actually not bad.

96
00:03:48,830 --> 00:03:50,910
Do you want to change career paths
in the future?

97
00:03:51,140 --> 00:03:53,180
For now,
I'll probably stay in this industry.

98
00:03:53,180 --> 00:03:55,300
But I'm actually quite interested
in psychology.

99
00:03:56,590 --> 00:03:57,590
Then,

100
00:03:57,590 --> 00:03:58,790
when you study psychology,

101
00:03:58,790 --> 00:04:00,870
what do you notice first about someone?

102
00:04:00,870 --> 00:04:01,620
(Curious)

103
00:04:02,380 --> 00:04:03,020
Their eyes.

104
00:04:03,020 --> 00:04:03,500
Their eyes?

105
00:04:04,030 --> 00:04:04,670
When I look at someone,

106
00:04:04,670 --> 00:04:06,390
I like looking into their eyes too.

107
00:04:07,060 --> 00:04:07,980
(Looks)

108
00:04:09,820 --> 00:04:10,620
(Laughing together)

109
00:04:12,030 --> 00:04:13,430
But I don't dare look into your eyes.

110
00:04:13,990 --> 00:04:14,990
I don't dare look into your eyes.

111
00:04:17,070 --> 00:04:19,470
(Stammering)
I'm... kind of afraid to.

112
00:04:20,190 --> 00:04:21,910
Because I'll read your mind?

113
00:04:22,430 --> 00:04:25,230
I can look into anyone else's eyes

114
00:04:25,910 --> 00:04:27,070
without looking away.

115
00:04:28,310 --> 00:04:30,870
But for some reason,

116
00:04:31,350 --> 00:04:32,270
I just feel like

117
00:04:32,270 --> 00:04:33,710
your eyes are like a "black hole".

118
00:04:34,430 --> 00:04:35,750
Your eyes are like a "black hole".

119
00:04:40,030 --> 00:04:41,590
Maybe they'll see right through you.

120
00:04:42,780 --> 00:04:43,500
Yeah.

121
00:04:45,510 --> 00:04:46,030
Xing,

122
00:04:46,030 --> 00:04:47,310
let's move the chairs over

123
00:04:47,310 --> 00:04:48,150
and take a photo together.

124
00:04:48,150 --> 00:04:48,500
Okay.

125
00:04:49,540 --> 00:04:52,270
Three, two, one.

126
00:04:54,230 --> 00:04:55,870
This one looks a little serious.

127
00:04:57,030 --> 00:04:57,590
Just a little.

128
00:04:57,950 --> 00:04:58,870
Which one do you like?

129
00:04:58,870 --> 00:04:59,430
What about you?

130
00:04:59,430 --> 00:05:00,750
I like this one.

131
00:05:01,380 --> 00:05:06,340
(Behind-the-Scenes 5)

132
00:05:06,750 --> 00:05:08,630
(Behind-the-Scenes)
Photo time.

133
00:05:08,950 --> 00:05:10,310
You guys took so many photos.

134
00:05:10,310 --> 00:05:11,110
Yeah.

135
00:05:11,590 --> 00:05:12,390
These look amazing.

136
00:05:12,790 --> 00:05:14,940
They really do.

137
00:05:16,110 --> 00:05:17,500
Let's take one of you two as well.

138
00:05:17,500 --> 00:05:18,580
Yeah, you two.

139
00:05:18,580 --> 00:05:18,910
Okay.

140
00:05:18,910 --> 00:05:19,670
Give us the blanket,

141
00:05:19,670 --> 00:05:20,460
then you two take one.

142
00:05:20,460 --> 00:05:20,820
Okay.

143
00:05:20,820 --> 00:05:21,390
You two go first.

144
00:05:22,110 --> 00:05:23,110
Another photo together.

145
00:05:23,110 --> 00:05:24,430
Any posing tips?

146
00:05:24,430 --> 00:05:25,230
No tips.

147
00:05:25,230 --> 00:05:26,830
Do you guys have any ideas?

148
00:05:29,100 --> 00:05:30,300
Yeah, this.

149
00:05:30,300 --> 00:05:31,510
This can be the "backdrop".

150
00:05:32,430 --> 00:05:33,510
This can be the "backdrop".

151
00:05:33,510 --> 00:05:34,270
Put it behind you two,

152
00:05:38,150 --> 00:05:39,510
then you two stand in front.

153
00:05:40,150 --> 00:05:40,470
Yeah.

154
00:05:40,470 --> 00:05:41,230
Like that.

155
00:05:41,780 --> 00:05:42,940
Okay.

156
00:05:42,940 --> 00:05:44,060
This looks like a proper show now.

157
00:05:44,060 --> 00:05:45,830
We'll hold the blanket up for you.

158
00:05:46,420 --> 00:05:47,260
(Helping Out)

159
00:05:47,310 --> 00:05:48,270
This is the "backdrop".

160
00:05:48,540 --> 00:05:49,270
Guess we'll do it like this.

161
00:05:49,270 --> 00:05:50,380
Here, pull it.

162
00:05:50,380 --> 00:05:51,820
(Enthusiastically helping)

163
00:05:52,750 --> 00:05:53,190
Not bad.

164
00:05:54,830 --> 00:05:55,310
Perhaps

165
00:05:55,310 --> 00:05:57,030
you guys could peek your heads
out a little.

166
00:05:57,030 --> 00:05:57,990
It'll look really good.

167
00:06:01,950 --> 00:06:02,180
You...

168
00:06:02,180 --> 00:06:05,710
Yeah.

169
00:06:06,030 --> 00:06:07,030
You're really putting on a show.

170
00:06:10,430 --> 00:06:11,420
So should we make funny faces,

171
00:06:11,420 --> 00:06:12,260
or what?

172
00:06:12,260 --> 00:06:13,220
Yeah, funny faces, obviously.

173
00:06:13,660 --> 00:06:14,260
Three,

174
00:06:14,660 --> 00:06:15,260
two,

175
00:06:15,860 --> 00:06:16,500
one.

176
00:06:20,140 --> 00:06:22,710
That looks so good!

177
00:06:22,710 --> 00:06:24,030
Only half his head is showing.

178
00:06:25,390 --> 00:06:26,550
Sorry, I kind of stole the spotlight.

179
00:06:26,550 --> 00:06:28,310
I didn't mean to.

180
00:06:28,310 --> 00:06:29,670
He's such a scene-stealer.

181
00:06:30,910 --> 00:06:31,830
No, we agreed earlier

182
00:06:31,830 --> 00:06:33,470
that all three of us
would make funny faces.

183
00:06:33,470 --> 00:06:34,870
(Smile / Pout / Funny Face)

184
00:06:34,870 --> 00:06:36,430
And I was the only one who listened.

185
00:06:36,670 --> 00:06:37,510
Yeah, and then someone

186
00:06:37,510 --> 00:06:38,750
started acting cute, you know?

187
00:06:39,150 --> 00:06:40,620
You were acting cute.

188
00:06:41,430 --> 00:06:42,270
No, I wasn't.

189
00:06:42,270 --> 00:06:43,500
I just froze like that.

190
00:06:45,510 --> 00:06:47,030
Quick, stick it on the fridge.

191
00:06:47,030 --> 00:06:48,860
We've filled the fridge in just one day.

192
00:06:48,860 --> 00:06:49,540
If we keep taking photos,

193
00:06:49,540 --> 00:06:51,430
we'll need to buy a magnetic wall.

194
00:06:51,430 --> 00:06:52,350
Seriously.

195
00:06:55,780 --> 00:07:00,740
(Behind-the-Scenes 6)

196
00:07:00,740 --> 00:07:02,020
(Behind-the-Scenes)
Let's go pay.

197
00:07:02,020 --> 00:07:02,900
Okay.

198
00:07:04,750 --> 00:07:05,790
Let's go.

199
00:07:11,590 --> 00:07:12,870
So normally,

200
00:07:12,870 --> 00:07:13,870
the exercise you do

201
00:07:13,870 --> 00:07:15,310
is mostly walking and badminton?

202
00:07:15,310 --> 00:07:15,900
(Curious)

203
00:07:17,260 --> 00:07:18,220
Pretty much.

204
00:07:18,220 --> 00:07:19,350
I used to

205
00:07:19,580 --> 00:07:20,140
go swimming too.

206
00:07:21,180 --> 00:07:22,060
Swimming?

207
00:07:22,630 --> 00:07:24,990
You quite like water sports?

208
00:07:26,030 --> 00:07:27,550
I quite like them.

209
00:07:28,340 --> 00:07:30,500
(Nods)

210
00:07:31,750 --> 00:07:34,790
Are there any nearby cities
you really want to visit?

211
00:07:34,790 --> 00:07:35,300
(Eyeing)

212
00:07:35,500 --> 00:07:36,230
(Thinking)

213
00:07:36,230 --> 00:07:38,140
Maybe...

214
00:07:38,140 --> 00:07:38,620
Baoding.

215
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:39,860
(Eyeing)
Baoding?

216
00:07:39,990 --> 00:07:40,590
Sure.

217
00:07:40,590 --> 00:07:41,180
(Laughs)

218
00:07:41,340 --> 00:07:42,500
(Shy)

219
00:07:42,670 --> 00:07:44,750
Is there any city you want to visit?

220
00:07:45,110 --> 00:07:46,110
(Asking)
A city I want to visit?

221
00:07:46,110 --> 00:07:47,820
Or somewhere you're curious about.

222
00:07:47,820 --> 00:07:48,620
Curious about?

223
00:07:49,110 --> 00:07:50,510
"The Center of the Universe",

224
00:07:50,510 --> 00:07:50,980
Tieling.

225
00:07:54,750 --> 00:07:55,870
(Laughs)
Don't copy me.

226
00:07:56,900 --> 00:07:57,220
I'm serious.

227
00:07:57,220 --> 00:07:58,060
I really mean it.

228
00:07:59,500 --> 00:08:04,420
(Behind-the-Scenes 7)

229
00:08:04,710 --> 00:08:05,750
(Behind-the-Scenes)
I remember you're from Shandong?

230
00:08:06,020 --> 00:08:06,630
Yeah.

231
00:08:06,630 --> 00:08:07,900
Then as someone from Shandong,

232
00:08:07,900 --> 00:08:09,550
don't you like braised pork and stuff?

233
00:08:09,950 --> 00:08:11,390
I can only eat a little.

234
00:08:11,390 --> 00:08:12,750
If I eat a whole piece,

235
00:08:12,750 --> 00:08:13,990
it gets too greasy for me.

236
00:08:13,990 --> 00:08:15,390
Yeah, it can be a bit greasy.

237
00:08:15,550 --> 00:08:17,630
Whenever I ate it before,
I'd remove the fatty parts.

238
00:08:17,780 --> 00:08:19,100
Me too.

239
00:08:19,380 --> 00:08:20,100
(Smiles)

240
00:08:20,270 --> 00:08:21,910
I really like Taizhou cuisine.

241
00:08:23,030 --> 00:08:24,270
What kind of food do they have?

242
00:08:24,270 --> 00:08:26,710
A lot of really light dishes.

243
00:08:26,710 --> 00:08:28,310
You should look it up.

244
00:08:29,350 --> 00:08:31,070
I remember you like lighter food too.

245
00:08:31,340 --> 00:08:31,940
Yeah.

246
00:08:31,940 --> 00:08:34,310
I honestly feel like every day we spend
in the house

247
00:08:34,310 --> 00:08:35,590
is one less day we have left.

248
00:08:35,590 --> 00:08:37,750
So every day after work,
I just want to hurry back here.

249
00:08:37,990 --> 00:08:39,910
Yeah. Every day in the house
brings a different surprise.

250
00:08:40,470 --> 00:08:42,470
I honestly don't even want
to go to sleep at night.

251
00:08:42,470 --> 00:08:44,150
That's exactly how I feel right now.

252
00:08:44,150 --> 00:08:45,950
And everyone here is so different.

253
00:08:46,620 --> 00:08:48,220
Everyone is

254
00:08:48,220 --> 00:08:49,230
kind and warm,

255
00:08:49,230 --> 00:08:51,550
but they each
have their own distinct personality.

256
00:08:52,030 --> 00:08:52,830
Yeah.

257
00:08:55,500 --> 00:09:00,460
(Behind-the-Scenes 8)

258
00:09:00,500 --> 00:09:03,980
(Behind-the-Scenes)

259
00:09:03,980 --> 00:09:05,230
You guys went
to get the polaroid camera?

260
00:09:05,230 --> 00:09:05,750
Yeah.

261
00:09:05,750 --> 00:09:07,230
Do you want to take a photo?

262
00:09:07,820 --> 00:09:08,900
(Looks)

263
00:09:10,910 --> 00:09:12,350
Let's take one of those two first.

264
00:09:12,350 --> 00:09:13,070
Take one of us two.

265
00:09:13,070 --> 00:09:13,460
Come on.

266
00:09:13,460 --> 00:09:13,980
Okay.

267
00:09:14,900 --> 00:09:17,060
Here we go. One, two, three.

268
00:09:19,260 --> 00:09:20,060
Done.

269
00:09:20,060 --> 00:09:20,950
(Stares)
Thanks, Si.

270
00:09:20,950 --> 00:09:21,620
No problem.

271
00:09:22,750 --> 00:09:23,030
Let me see.

272
00:09:23,900 --> 00:09:24,580
Wait.

273
00:09:25,310 --> 00:09:25,990
Then...

274
00:09:26,950 --> 00:09:28,180
(Looks)
Xing and I

275
00:09:28,180 --> 00:09:28,990
haven't taken one together yet.

276
00:09:28,990 --> 00:09:29,470
Right.

277
00:09:29,470 --> 00:09:30,750
I'll take one of you two.

278
00:09:30,750 --> 00:09:31,430
Okay.

279
00:09:31,430 --> 00:09:32,390
But I think it's a little too bright...

280
00:09:32,390 --> 00:09:32,790
How about this?

281
00:09:33,270 --> 00:09:35,150
I'll take one of you three,

282
00:09:35,150 --> 00:09:36,420
then you take one of us three.

283
00:09:36,420 --> 00:09:37,340
Okay.

284
00:09:37,340 --> 00:09:38,710
Take one of us two first.

285
00:09:38,710 --> 00:09:39,470
Sure, no problem.

286
00:09:39,470 --> 00:09:40,220
(Moves Closer)

287
00:09:40,510 --> 00:09:42,270
Actually,
I think you could stand over there.

288
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:45,100
Come on.

289
00:09:45,100 --> 00:09:47,740
One, two, three.

290
00:09:50,230 --> 00:09:52,390
Let me see the one we just took.

291
00:09:52,390 --> 00:09:54,430
I look a little bad.

292
00:09:56,390 --> 00:09:57,700
Can we take another one?

293
00:09:57,700 --> 00:09:59,350
Xing and I will take another.

294
00:09:59,350 --> 00:09:59,660
Sure.

295
00:09:59,660 --> 00:10:00,140
Okay.

296
00:10:03,060 --> 00:10:04,060
Let's change spots.

297
00:10:04,060 --> 00:10:05,190
(Suggesting)
You can go over there too.

298
00:10:05,430 --> 00:10:06,390
Here works too.

299
00:10:07,020 --> 00:10:08,300
You can sit down for it.

300
00:10:08,300 --> 00:10:08,990
Sure.

301
00:10:12,230 --> 00:10:13,630
Try to look a little more natural.

302
00:10:15,790 --> 00:10:16,910
Yeah, look how relaxed he is.

303
00:10:16,910 --> 00:10:17,510
You can learn from him.

304
00:10:17,510 --> 00:10:18,750
No, I just...

305
00:10:19,410 --> 00:10:20,380
Okay.

306
00:10:23,750 --> 00:10:24,590
There's one more, right?

307
00:10:24,590 --> 00:10:24,870
Yeah.

308
00:10:24,870 --> 00:10:25,510
One of us two.

309
00:10:25,510 --> 00:10:25,740
Okay.

310
00:10:25,740 --> 00:10:26,540
Sure.

311
00:10:26,540 --> 00:10:26,950
No problem.

312
00:10:29,670 --> 00:10:31,180
Yeah, sit over here.

313
00:10:31,910 --> 00:10:33,310
Let me see
if I should take it horizontally or...

314
00:10:34,790 --> 00:10:35,590
Peace signs.

315
00:10:35,980 --> 00:10:36,590
Sure.

316
00:10:36,590 --> 00:10:37,550
Yeah, just relax.

317
00:10:37,550 --> 00:10:38,670
Pose however you want.

318
00:10:38,670 --> 00:10:38,990
Right.

319
00:10:39,180 --> 00:10:40,100
Three,

320
00:10:40,100 --> 00:10:40,900
two,

321
00:10:40,900 --> 00:10:41,410
one.

322
00:10:44,910 --> 00:10:45,950
This one looks really good.

323
00:10:46,070 --> 00:10:47,540
I quite like it.

324
00:10:47,540 --> 00:10:48,380
I like it too.

325
00:10:49,070 --> 00:10:49,830
In this photo today,

326
00:10:49,830 --> 00:10:50,950
you kind of look like a "girl boss".

327
00:10:51,550 --> 00:10:53,660
That's my "girl boss" look today.

328
00:10:53,660 --> 00:10:54,230
Don't you think so?

329
00:10:54,230 --> 00:10:55,430
You really do look like
a "girl boss" today.

330
00:10:55,430 --> 00:10:56,470
Definitely "girl boss" vibes.

331
00:10:58,950 --> 00:10:59,830
This photo looks really good.

332
00:10:59,830 --> 00:11:00,550
I really like this one.

333
00:11:06,180 --> 00:11:11,140
(Behind-the-Scenes 9)

334
00:11:11,630 --> 00:11:13,390
(Wu Xingying & Sun Bohan's city date)
Xing, which one do you like best?

335
00:11:13,710 --> 00:11:15,300
This is my favorite photo
of us together.

336
00:11:15,700 --> 00:11:16,340
(Moves Closer)
This one?

337
00:11:16,780 --> 00:11:17,390
This one of you?

338
00:11:17,390 --> 00:11:18,750
Because of the lighting.

339
00:11:19,070 --> 00:11:19,990
I think so too.

340
00:11:21,230 --> 00:11:22,110
I'll drive first.

341
00:11:22,110 --> 00:11:22,620
Okay.

342
00:11:24,340 --> 00:11:25,460
(Glances)

343
00:11:25,700 --> 00:11:27,180
You look really beautiful today.

344
00:11:27,180 --> 00:11:27,740
(Shy)

345
00:11:27,740 --> 00:11:28,950
(Admiring her)
You look really beautiful today.

346
00:11:30,750 --> 00:11:32,550
The scenery here is beautiful too.

347
00:11:33,110 --> 00:11:34,100
(Mishears)
It's because the sunlight

348
00:11:34,100 --> 00:11:34,660
is really nice here.

349
00:11:35,230 --> 00:11:35,900
It's the person.

350
00:11:36,230 --> 00:11:38,790
The person
makes the scenery look even better.

351
00:11:46,990 --> 00:11:47,470
Okay.

352
00:11:48,550 --> 00:11:49,150
Candid shot.

353
00:11:50,740 --> 00:11:51,420
Xing,

354
00:11:51,420 --> 00:11:52,830
when you travel,

355
00:11:52,990 --> 00:11:55,990
do you prefer planning everything out,

356
00:11:55,990 --> 00:11:57,230
or just going with the flow?

357
00:11:58,830 --> 00:12:00,470
I'm more of a go-with-the-flow person.

358
00:12:00,470 --> 00:12:01,430
Actually, me too.

359
00:12:01,430 --> 00:12:03,470
I might set a rough framework.

360
00:12:04,030 --> 00:12:05,910
I think
having a general direction is enough.

361
00:12:06,190 --> 00:12:07,870
For everything else,
I'd rather slowly explore as I go.

362
00:12:07,870 --> 00:12:08,260
Yeah.

363
00:12:09,270 --> 00:12:11,150
I think the two of us

364
00:12:11,670 --> 00:12:13,590
are pretty similar in that way.

365
00:12:14,390 --> 00:12:16,350
We like unexpected surprises.

366
00:12:16,460 --> 00:12:16,860
Yeah.

367
00:12:16,860 --> 00:12:17,380
Right?

368
00:12:17,380 --> 00:12:17,990
(Liking unexpected surprises)

369
00:12:17,990 --> 00:12:18,470
Mm-hmm.

370
00:12:22,980 --> 00:12:27,940
(Behind-the-Scenes 10)

371
00:12:27,980 --> 00:12:31,900
(Behind-the-Scenes)

372
00:12:31,900 --> 00:12:33,300
Come try some.

373
00:12:33,300 --> 00:12:33,940
Smells amazing.

374
00:12:34,550 --> 00:12:36,500
I could already smell it from far away.

375
00:12:36,500 --> 00:12:38,180
I'm not hungry, so I won't eat yet.

376
00:12:39,030 --> 00:12:40,460
Are you guys really not hungry?

377
00:12:40,460 --> 00:12:41,140
Yeah.

378
00:12:41,630 --> 00:12:42,900
You guys hurry up and eat.

379
00:12:42,900 --> 00:12:43,700
Okay.

380
00:12:45,230 --> 00:12:46,270
You can sit in my seat.

381
00:12:46,270 --> 00:12:46,950
I'm full.

382
00:12:46,950 --> 00:12:48,350
You guys sit down.

383
00:12:48,910 --> 00:12:50,070
Take my little bowl.

384
00:12:50,070 --> 00:12:50,700
(Stands up)

385
00:12:50,790 --> 00:12:51,870
Sit down, Si.

386
00:12:51,870 --> 00:12:52,710
Thanks.

387
00:12:52,710 --> 00:12:54,230
We can sit here.

388
00:12:54,230 --> 00:12:55,510
They've finished eating.

389
00:12:59,470 --> 00:13:01,190
Did Cui Yihang make this?

390
00:13:01,190 --> 00:13:02,470
Probably.

391
00:13:08,350 --> 00:13:09,500
Have you eaten?

392
00:13:09,820 --> 00:13:10,590
Yeah.

393
00:13:10,590 --> 00:13:11,670
Did you make this?

394
00:13:12,100 --> 00:13:12,460
Yeah.

395
00:13:15,700 --> 00:13:16,380
(Smiles)

396
00:13:16,380 --> 00:13:17,060
(Holding it in)

397
00:13:21,150 --> 00:13:21,870
Stop holding back your smile.

398
00:13:25,140 --> 00:13:30,100
(Behind-the-Scenes 11)

399
00:13:30,140 --> 00:13:32,940
(Behind-the-Scenes)

400
00:13:32,940 --> 00:13:35,950
I remember
my mom makes dumplings with spinach,

401
00:13:37,230 --> 00:13:39,100
vermicelli,

402
00:13:39,100 --> 00:13:40,100
wood ear mushrooms...

403
00:13:40,100 --> 00:13:40,860
Yeah?

404
00:13:40,860 --> 00:13:41,540
And egg.

405
00:13:42,030 --> 00:13:42,870
They're delicious.

406
00:13:42,870 --> 00:13:44,710
Spinach, vermicelli, wood ear mushrooms,

407
00:13:45,070 --> 00:13:45,510
and egg?

408
00:13:45,510 --> 00:13:47,870
It's kind
of like three-delicacy dumplings.

409
00:13:48,030 --> 00:13:48,630
Yeah.

410
00:13:49,230 --> 00:13:50,230
You can make them without shrimp.

411
00:13:51,700 --> 00:13:52,500
(Smiles)

412
00:13:53,670 --> 00:13:55,310
(Joking)
Maybe you could challenge yourself?

413
00:13:55,310 --> 00:13:56,070
Maybe one day you'll...

414
00:13:56,070 --> 00:13:56,590
No.

415
00:13:56,590 --> 00:13:57,180
...stop being allergic.

416
00:13:57,180 --> 00:13:57,860
No.

417
00:13:59,350 --> 00:14:01,390
(Concerned)
Let's not do anything risky.

418
00:14:03,270 --> 00:14:04,230
We can make...

419
00:14:04,790 --> 00:14:05,580
Make...

420
00:14:06,630 --> 00:14:07,750
"Mock crab".

421
00:14:07,790 --> 00:14:08,590
I know that dish.

422
00:14:08,860 --> 00:14:09,870
It's so good.

423
00:14:10,350 --> 00:14:11,390
We can make it sometime.

424
00:14:12,910 --> 00:14:13,830
But I don't know how yet.

425
00:14:13,830 --> 00:14:14,910
We can use a cheat sheet next time.

426
00:14:16,030 --> 00:14:17,470
I can ask my dad.

427
00:14:17,910 --> 00:14:19,540
He's probably really good at making it.

428
00:14:19,540 --> 00:14:21,670
We can ask your dad
for his secret recipe.

429
00:14:23,510 --> 00:14:24,710
Can we eat it today?

430
00:14:24,910 --> 00:14:26,360
(Anytime)
Sure. If you want it,

431
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:27,540
you can have it anytime.

432
00:14:36,900 --> 00:14:41,860
(Behind-the-Scenes 12)

433
00:14:41,900 --> 00:14:43,900
(Behind-the-Scenes)

434
00:14:43,900 --> 00:14:47,140
(Writing)

435
00:14:56,830 --> 00:14:58,030
Why do you look so deep in thought?

436
00:14:58,030 --> 00:14:58,750
Deep in thought?

437
00:14:59,310 --> 00:15:00,910
What's wrong? What's going on?

438
00:15:00,910 --> 00:15:01,940
Something's up.

439
00:15:01,940 --> 00:15:02,900
No.

440
00:15:02,900 --> 00:15:04,620
Something's up.

441
00:15:04,900 --> 00:15:05,710
Definitely.

442
00:15:06,230 --> 00:15:07,150
Don't hide it from me.

443
00:15:08,110 --> 00:15:08,830
There really isn't.

444
00:15:09,110 --> 00:15:09,470
Nothing.

445
00:15:09,470 --> 00:15:10,830
I'm just trying to remember something.

446
00:15:10,830 --> 00:15:11,710
I'm afraid I'll forget it.

447
00:15:12,230 --> 00:15:13,430
Just a few things.

448
00:15:14,550 --> 00:15:15,430
Something really simple.

449
00:15:15,430 --> 00:15:17,270
(Little boat drifting along)
You rowed for quite a while today.

450
00:15:17,470 --> 00:15:17,790
Yeah.

451
00:15:17,790 --> 00:15:18,390
I realized that too.

452
00:15:18,390 --> 00:15:20,110
How long were we out there?

453
00:15:21,070 --> 00:15:23,230
You either don't go boating at all,

454
00:15:23,230 --> 00:15:25,110
or once you do, you never come back.

455
00:15:26,510 --> 00:15:26,790
Yeah.

456
00:15:26,790 --> 00:15:28,270
I feel like we ate pretty early,

457
00:15:28,270 --> 00:15:30,350
and then we went boating

458
00:15:31,870 --> 00:15:33,630
with no intention of coming back.

459
00:15:35,310 --> 00:15:36,430
But the trip back was pretty quick.

460
00:15:36,430 --> 00:15:37,870
It went smoothly, with the current.

461
00:15:38,550 --> 00:15:40,710
On the way there, everything felt new,
and we could barely get the boat moving.

462
00:15:40,710 --> 00:15:42,030
It was pretty fun.

463
00:15:42,030 --> 00:15:43,430
The surroundings
were actually really nice.

464
00:15:43,430 --> 00:15:45,590
I originally wanted
to come back early today,

465
00:15:45,590 --> 00:15:46,580
but then we went

466
00:15:46,580 --> 00:15:47,420
to the supermarket.

467
00:15:47,950 --> 00:15:49,230
Was the supermarket fun, Yu Yang?

468
00:15:49,950 --> 00:15:51,110
Yeah, grocery shopping was pretty fun.

469
00:15:52,310 --> 00:15:53,830
I haven't been anywhere yet.

470
00:15:54,150 --> 00:15:55,230
The supermarket was

471
00:15:56,150 --> 00:15:57,110
pretty crowded.

472
00:15:57,990 --> 00:15:58,830
It was nice.

473
00:16:01,150 --> 00:16:02,790
I talked for so long
and still can't remember anything.

474
00:16:04,230 --> 00:16:05,270
I only remember these few words.

475
00:16:05,270 --> 00:16:05,780
(Si / Tian)

476
00:16:07,460 --> 00:16:07,670
No.

477
00:16:07,670 --> 00:16:09,550
As long
as you remember the overall feeling,

478
00:16:09,550 --> 00:16:11,180
that's enough.

479
00:16:11,470 --> 00:16:12,380
Yeah, that's good.

480
00:16:12,380 --> 00:16:14,110
Just remember the important parts.

481
00:16:18,060 --> 00:16:23,020
(Behind-the-Scenes 13)

482
00:16:23,060 --> 00:16:24,740
(Wu Xingying & Sun Bohan's city date)

483
00:16:24,740 --> 00:16:25,460
That day,

484
00:16:25,460 --> 00:16:27,390
you and Si
entered the house together, right?

485
00:16:27,870 --> 00:16:29,390
Yeah, we came in together that day.

486
00:16:30,150 --> 00:16:31,830
Actually, I asked Si

487
00:16:31,830 --> 00:16:33,390
to bring the polaroid camera
and help take a photo of us.

488
00:16:33,710 --> 00:16:34,750
But after dinner,

489
00:16:35,350 --> 00:16:36,990
I realized you'd disappeared.

490
00:16:37,870 --> 00:16:39,430
That's because earlier,

491
00:16:39,430 --> 00:16:40,420
Sha Yue'er and I went boating together.

492
00:16:41,510 --> 00:16:43,670
We were basically just

493
00:16:44,270 --> 00:16:45,270
chatting,

494
00:16:45,270 --> 00:16:47,350
like friends do.

495
00:16:48,150 --> 00:16:48,510
Yeah.

496
00:16:49,710 --> 00:16:51,710
I wonder if Si went boating today.

497
00:16:52,190 --> 00:16:54,390
I guess she probably did.

498
00:16:54,470 --> 00:16:55,990
You have no idea
how funny it was yesterday.

499
00:16:55,990 --> 00:16:57,230
The two of us went boating, right?

500
00:16:57,390 --> 00:16:58,550
Zhao Xilun saw us too.

501
00:16:59,150 --> 00:17:01,540
And right away he said,

502
00:17:01,540 --> 00:17:02,460
"Boating again?"

503
00:17:02,910 --> 00:17:04,110
Said that I'm the "Boat King".

504
00:17:05,190 --> 00:17:06,550
Boat King, boating out there every day.

505
00:17:06,790 --> 00:17:08,590
If you're not boating at sea,

506
00:17:08,590 --> 00:17:09,620
(Joking)
you'd be the "Sea King".

507
00:17:09,620 --> 00:17:09,900
Yeah.

508
00:17:09,900 --> 00:17:10,820
Boating yesterday,

509
00:17:10,820 --> 00:17:11,830
and boating again today.

510
00:17:11,830 --> 00:17:12,830
I practically live on that boat.

511
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:19,660
(Behind-the-Scenes 14)

512
00:17:20,300 --> 00:17:21,380
(Behind-the-Scenes)
What are you doing?

513
00:17:21,380 --> 00:17:23,430
I'm helping Yu Yang mix the filling.

514
00:17:23,670 --> 00:17:24,780
Want to stir it for a while?

515
00:17:24,780 --> 00:17:25,660
It's actually pretty fun.

516
00:17:25,780 --> 00:17:26,300
Sure.

517
00:17:28,150 --> 00:17:29,110
Here, I'll do it.

518
00:17:29,150 --> 00:17:30,190
Here, I'll hold it for you.

519
00:17:30,190 --> 00:17:30,790
Just stir.

520
00:17:30,790 --> 00:17:31,230
It's pretty hard.

521
00:17:31,350 --> 00:17:32,470
Keep stirring counterclockwise.

522
00:17:32,660 --> 00:17:33,470
(Holding)

523
00:17:33,470 --> 00:17:34,620
Why can't I stir clockwise?

524
00:17:34,620 --> 00:17:35,980
Because you need
to keep stirring in one direction.

525
00:17:35,980 --> 00:17:37,190
It'll come together faster that way.

526
00:17:37,190 --> 00:17:38,710
You're so smart.

527
00:17:40,750 --> 00:17:42,150
(Lifts)
Why does this feel kind of difficult?

528
00:17:42,150 --> 00:17:42,980
Want me to do it?

529
00:17:42,980 --> 00:17:43,380
Okay.

530
00:17:43,380 --> 00:17:44,020
Don't...

531
00:17:44,020 --> 00:17:44,670
Why don't you do it?

532
00:17:47,340 --> 00:17:49,420
Let's make dumplings.

533
00:17:49,420 --> 00:17:49,940
I'm here.

534
00:17:50,510 --> 00:17:51,150
It's not very sticky.

535
00:17:51,150 --> 00:17:52,030
I'll put a bowl of water here.

536
00:17:52,030 --> 00:17:52,860
They aren't sticking very well.

537
00:17:52,860 --> 00:17:54,100
Can everyone reach it?
I'll leave it here.

538
00:17:54,100 --> 00:17:54,660
Yeah.

539
00:17:57,260 --> 00:17:57,700
(Frowns)

540
00:17:57,700 --> 00:17:59,230
This won't close at all.

541
00:17:59,830 --> 00:18:01,430
You didn't use enough water.

542
00:18:01,910 --> 00:18:02,820
Like this?

543
00:18:02,820 --> 00:18:03,950
Yeah, it's not sticky enough.

544
00:18:04,550 --> 00:18:05,670
But the shape looks pretty good.

545
00:18:05,750 --> 00:18:06,710
Maybe you need more water.

546
00:18:06,710 --> 00:18:08,510
These wrappers were machine-made.

547
00:18:09,950 --> 00:18:10,750
The shape looks good.

548
00:18:11,620 --> 00:18:12,260
(Looks)

549
00:18:13,430 --> 00:18:14,230
I think I'll just leave mine

550
00:18:14,230 --> 00:18:14,870
like this.

551
00:18:16,740 --> 00:18:18,420
(Laughs)

552
00:18:19,030 --> 00:18:20,310
Have you made dumplings before?

553
00:18:20,420 --> 00:18:21,740
Yeah.

554
00:18:22,070 --> 00:18:23,470
Isn't mine cute?

555
00:18:24,180 --> 00:18:24,860
(Nods)

556
00:18:33,660 --> 00:18:38,620
(Behind-the-Scenes 15)

557
00:18:38,660 --> 00:18:39,300
(Behind-the-Scenes)

558
00:18:39,300 --> 00:18:40,190
Let's go shopping.

559
00:18:40,990 --> 00:18:42,350
Have you decided what to buy?

560
00:18:43,380 --> 00:18:44,540
(Looks)

561
00:18:45,430 --> 00:18:46,270
Fragrant lemons.

562
00:18:47,070 --> 00:18:48,550
Let's get some other fruit too.

563
00:18:48,550 --> 00:18:50,350
Okay, let's grab a cart.

564
00:18:54,900 --> 00:18:55,980
(Stops)

565
00:18:55,980 --> 00:18:56,820
Let's have a look.

566
00:18:57,870 --> 00:18:59,230
Could I get some ground beef?

567
00:18:59,230 --> 00:19:00,950
I'm just making mapo tofu,

568
00:19:00,950 --> 00:19:01,590
so I only need a little.

569
00:19:03,190 --> 00:19:04,390
A small piece is enough.

570
00:19:04,390 --> 00:19:05,780
Yeah, just this much.

571
00:19:06,340 --> 00:19:06,620
Enough?

572
00:19:06,790 --> 00:19:07,590
Yeah.

573
00:19:07,780 --> 00:19:09,220
Grind it once.

574
00:19:09,740 --> 00:19:10,380
Okay.

575
00:19:10,380 --> 00:19:11,100
Thank you.

576
00:19:12,900 --> 00:19:13,780
Knife-cut noodles.

577
00:19:14,990 --> 00:19:16,100
I want knife-cut noodles.

578
00:19:16,100 --> 00:19:16,460
Sure.

579
00:19:16,460 --> 00:19:16,940
(Wants some)

580
00:19:17,150 --> 00:19:17,990
Let's get another pack.

581
00:19:17,990 --> 00:19:18,350
Okay.

582
00:19:21,020 --> 00:19:21,500
This one.

583
00:19:21,830 --> 00:19:22,070
Enough.

584
00:19:22,180 --> 00:19:22,780
One is enough.

585
00:19:23,110 --> 00:19:23,550
Okay.

586
00:19:23,900 --> 00:19:26,300
Those croissants we had last time
were pretty good.

587
00:19:26,470 --> 00:19:27,380
I want another box.

588
00:19:27,380 --> 00:19:28,180
Okay.

589
00:19:28,180 --> 00:19:28,940
(Turns and follows)

590
00:19:28,940 --> 00:19:29,830
Croissants

591
00:19:31,310 --> 00:19:32,230
are sold out.

592
00:19:33,070 --> 00:19:34,350
Then let's get something else.

593
00:19:34,350 --> 00:19:35,060
Oat bread.

594
00:19:35,310 --> 00:19:36,390
This looks good

595
00:19:36,390 --> 00:19:37,390
and healthy too.

596
00:19:37,830 --> 00:19:39,270
You can heat this one up.

597
00:19:39,950 --> 00:19:41,220
This one looks tasty too.

598
00:19:41,220 --> 00:19:42,150
Let's get one of these as well.

599
00:19:42,150 --> 00:19:42,950
This one? Okay.

600
00:19:42,950 --> 00:19:45,110
This looks like
it'd be really good dipped in yogurt.

601
00:19:48,820 --> 00:19:49,740
(Takes it)

602
00:19:52,150 --> 00:19:52,950
Perfect.

603
00:19:54,140 --> 00:19:55,380
I'll carry one.

604
00:19:56,750 --> 00:19:58,190
It's okay, I've got it. Let's go.

605
00:19:58,190 --> 00:19:59,350
I'll support it from underneath.

606
00:19:59,980 --> 00:20:00,620
Okay, you can carry it.

607
00:20:00,620 --> 00:20:02,230
Here, you can carry one side.

608
00:20:02,830 --> 00:20:03,620
Let's go.

609
00:20:03,620 --> 00:20:05,060
(Carrying together)

610
00:20:05,620 --> 00:20:07,060
Alright, let's go.

611
00:20:09,260 --> 00:20:14,220
(Behind-the-Scenes 16)

612
00:20:14,710 --> 00:20:15,950
(Behind-the-Scenes)
I can actually eat more than you.

613
00:20:16,550 --> 00:20:17,630
I've just been holding back.

614
00:20:18,790 --> 00:20:20,070
Why? Afraid of gaining weight?

615
00:20:20,830 --> 00:20:21,190
Yeah.

616
00:20:21,630 --> 00:20:22,660
I've already given up on dieting.

617
00:20:22,980 --> 00:20:24,230
I give up on diets really quickly.

618
00:20:24,710 --> 00:20:26,030
Losing weight is really hard for me too.

619
00:20:27,110 --> 00:20:29,380
When I gain weight,
it shows on my face first.

620
00:20:29,380 --> 00:20:30,910
And when I lose weight,
it is the last place to slim down.

621
00:20:33,340 --> 00:20:34,420
(Looks)

622
00:20:37,310 --> 00:20:39,310
I think you'd still look good
with a slightly fuller face.

623
00:20:42,860 --> 00:20:43,900
(Puffs cheeks)

624
00:20:49,230 --> 00:20:50,670
I don't think I can eat anymore.

625
00:20:51,070 --> 00:20:52,230
Okay, then don't.

626
00:20:52,230 --> 00:20:53,310
Just put it over here.

627
00:20:53,900 --> 00:20:55,460
(Moves food)

628
00:21:01,830 --> 00:21:03,670
Gotta replenish all that lost protein.

629
00:21:03,910 --> 00:21:05,310
Might as well replenish tomorrow's too.

630
00:21:07,150 --> 00:21:08,870
You're making it sound like
we won't have food tomorrow.

631
00:21:14,100 --> 00:21:19,060
(Behind-the-Scenes 17)

632
00:21:19,100 --> 00:21:23,740
(Behind-the-Scenes)

633
00:21:23,740 --> 00:21:24,420
That sounds really nice.

634
00:21:25,790 --> 00:21:26,740
Want to play for a bit?

635
00:21:26,940 --> 00:21:28,180
I don't know how.

636
00:21:29,310 --> 00:21:31,270
I'd rather just listen.

637
00:21:31,270 --> 00:21:32,180
I tried learning before.

638
00:21:32,180 --> 00:21:33,830
Honestly,
I really have no talent for this.

639
00:21:33,830 --> 00:21:34,710
Come on.

640
00:21:34,710 --> 00:21:36,110
Play "Two Tigers" for us.

641
00:21:37,430 --> 00:21:37,990
I don't remember it.

642
00:21:37,990 --> 00:21:38,710
Can you teach me again?

643
00:21:38,710 --> 00:21:39,430
Sure, come on.

644
00:21:40,430 --> 00:21:41,470
I remember it being really simple.

645
00:21:44,110 --> 00:21:45,270
Wasn't that
"Twinkle, Twinkle, Little Star"?

646
00:21:45,270 --> 00:21:46,830
Yeah.
I think that's what I played back then.

647
00:21:47,110 --> 00:21:48,260
(Laughs)
Not "Two Tigers".

648
00:21:48,260 --> 00:21:49,110
"Two Tigers" goes...

649
00:21:49,110 --> 00:21:50,550
♪Two tigers♪

650
00:21:50,550 --> 00:21:51,420
It was definitely

651
00:21:51,420 --> 00:21:52,070
"Twinkle, Little Star".

652
00:21:52,070 --> 00:21:53,670
Then want to try playing it?

653
00:21:54,430 --> 00:21:55,550
I don't remember it anymore, teacher.

654
00:22:01,940 --> 00:22:04,260
(Focused)

655
00:22:08,590 --> 00:22:09,590
This one, right?

656
00:22:12,420 --> 00:22:13,220
Yeah.

657
00:22:13,820 --> 00:22:14,620
(Applause)

658
00:22:14,910 --> 00:22:15,860
Great teaching, teacher.

659
00:22:15,860 --> 00:22:16,660
Seriously...

660
00:22:17,590 --> 00:22:18,590
I spent an entire lesson

661
00:22:18,590 --> 00:22:19,870
and only learned this little bit.

662
00:22:22,220 --> 00:22:27,180
(Behind-the-Scenes 18)

663
00:22:27,220 --> 00:22:28,620
(Behind-the-Scenes)

664
00:22:28,620 --> 00:22:29,910
Do your parents usually

665
00:22:29,910 --> 00:22:32,190
go for walks with you?

666
00:22:33,300 --> 00:22:34,020
Yeah.

667
00:22:34,750 --> 00:22:35,670
Then who usually initiates

668
00:22:35,670 --> 00:22:37,110
your daily video calls?

669
00:22:40,190 --> 00:22:41,030
It depends.

670
00:22:41,030 --> 00:22:42,100
But I think

671
00:22:42,100 --> 00:22:43,340
my parents probably call me more often.

672
00:22:43,340 --> 00:22:44,670
They're usually the ones who call first.

673
00:22:46,350 --> 00:22:48,020
Do you ever call them first?

674
00:22:48,020 --> 00:22:48,460
Yeah.

675
00:22:48,460 --> 00:22:50,830
Whenever we have free time,

676
00:22:50,830 --> 00:22:51,870
we're almost always on the phone.

677
00:22:52,510 --> 00:22:54,340
So you share everything with them?

678
00:22:54,340 --> 00:22:54,820
Yeah.

679
00:22:55,030 --> 00:22:55,630
Pretty much.

680
00:22:55,990 --> 00:22:57,790
Even things about your relationships?

681
00:22:57,790 --> 00:22:58,460
(Curious)

682
00:22:59,510 --> 00:23:00,710
Yeah, I talk to them about that too.

683
00:23:00,710 --> 00:23:01,990
Do your parents

684
00:23:01,990 --> 00:23:04,270
give you advice and things like that?

685
00:23:04,950 --> 00:23:05,390
Not really,

686
00:23:05,630 --> 00:23:06,740
because I already know

687
00:23:06,740 --> 00:23:08,820
how they'll view something

688
00:23:09,030 --> 00:23:10,590
and where they're coming from.

689
00:23:10,630 --> 00:23:12,950
So you have a relationship
based on mutual respect?

690
00:23:13,510 --> 00:23:15,430
Respect is definitely essential.

691
00:23:15,430 --> 00:23:17,750
We see each individual

692
00:23:17,750 --> 00:23:19,230
as part of

693
00:23:20,070 --> 00:23:20,710
a greater whole.

694
00:23:22,070 --> 00:23:23,030
We're one big family,

695
00:23:23,030 --> 00:23:24,830
with each of us branching out
from there.

696
00:23:24,830 --> 00:23:26,310
Whenever something comes up,
we'll discuss it together.

697
00:23:26,310 --> 00:23:27,110
I share

698
00:23:27,110 --> 00:23:28,310
my personal thoughts with them too.

699
00:23:28,310 --> 00:23:29,190
Some of my thoughts

700
00:23:29,190 --> 00:23:30,790
are more work-related,

701
00:23:31,540 --> 00:23:35,260
like how I approach things
and how I see the world.

702
00:23:35,350 --> 00:23:36,550
After I share those things with them,

703
00:23:36,550 --> 00:23:38,590
they might feel that I'm growing

704
00:23:38,590 --> 00:23:39,070
and more mature.

705
00:23:39,070 --> 00:23:41,870
That puts their minds at ease.

706
00:23:41,870 --> 00:23:42,950
That's why I share these things.

707
00:23:43,190 --> 00:23:44,790
That's quite special.

708
00:23:45,510 --> 00:23:46,470
From how you describe it,

709
00:23:46,470 --> 00:23:48,310
it sounds like you and your parents
get along well like friends.

710
00:23:48,990 --> 00:23:49,830
Right?

711
00:23:50,020 --> 00:23:50,380
Yeah.

712
00:23:51,420 --> 00:23:56,380
(Behind-the-Scenes 19)

713
00:23:56,420 --> 00:24:01,220
(Behind-the-Scenes)

714
00:24:01,220 --> 00:24:02,260
(Sighs)

715
00:24:02,780 --> 00:24:03,660
(Concerned)

716
00:24:03,990 --> 00:24:04,950
What were you going to say?

717
00:24:04,950 --> 00:24:05,950
Nothing, I...

718
00:24:06,350 --> 00:24:07,470
I'm just worried about your foot.

719
00:24:09,470 --> 00:24:12,310
It's okay. I'll get it checked later.

720
00:24:12,310 --> 00:24:13,750
I'll take you now.

721
00:24:14,590 --> 00:24:15,590
Now?

722
00:24:16,100 --> 00:24:17,100
Let's get it checked.

723
00:24:17,100 --> 00:24:17,910
Okay.

724
00:24:18,190 --> 00:24:19,630
I really didn't notice just now.

725
00:24:20,150 --> 00:24:21,910
It's okay. We all had our eyes closed.

726
00:24:22,860 --> 00:24:23,420
I...

727
00:24:24,020 --> 00:24:25,020
It's fine.

728
00:24:25,020 --> 00:24:25,980
I didn't want to say anything.

729
00:24:25,980 --> 00:24:27,670
I just didn't want you

730
00:24:27,670 --> 00:24:29,270
to stay here like this, okay?

731
00:24:31,910 --> 00:24:32,790
It'll be fine once it's bandaged.

732
00:24:34,060 --> 00:24:34,620
I forgive you.

733
00:24:34,620 --> 00:24:35,900
(Feeling guilty)

734
00:24:38,030 --> 00:24:39,710
Your toenail looks a little...

735
00:24:39,710 --> 00:24:40,430
How did it happen?

736
00:24:40,710 --> 00:24:41,340
I kicked something.

737
00:24:41,340 --> 00:24:42,700
She kicked my shoe.

738
00:24:42,830 --> 00:24:45,190
She probably needs a bandage
or some disinfectant.

739
00:24:45,430 --> 00:24:46,100
All done.

740
00:24:46,100 --> 00:24:46,780
Does it hurt?

741
00:24:46,780 --> 00:24:48,550
Can a dancer be afraid of pain?

742
00:24:48,910 --> 00:24:49,710
Still...

743
00:24:55,620 --> 00:24:59,220
The medicine she put on
actually works pretty well.

744
00:24:59,220 --> 00:25:01,190
It doesn't hurt.

745
00:25:01,190 --> 00:25:02,310
It doesn't hurt anymore?

746
00:25:05,660 --> 00:25:06,900
(Sighs)

747
00:25:08,270 --> 00:25:09,110
No sighing.

748
00:25:13,390 --> 00:25:13,860
I sucked it back.

749
00:25:13,860 --> 00:25:14,420
It's gone.

750
00:25:18,110 --> 00:25:20,070
I've sucked back the sigh I let out.

751
00:25:20,820 --> 00:25:21,620
That's funny.

752
00:25:22,510 --> 00:25:24,630
Let's head back to the house.

753
00:25:27,300 --> 00:25:32,260
(Behind-the-Scenes 20)

754
00:25:32,260 --> 00:25:33,750
(Behind-the-Scenes)
I brought the polaroid camera over.

755
00:25:34,510 --> 00:25:35,750
I'll leave it here for you.

756
00:25:37,020 --> 00:25:38,910
Then help us take a photo.

757
00:25:38,910 --> 00:25:39,830
Sure.

758
00:25:39,990 --> 00:25:40,830
Let's each take one.

759
00:25:43,270 --> 00:25:44,710
Let me check the angle.

760
00:25:44,710 --> 00:25:45,590
Where would be a good spot?

761
00:25:45,590 --> 00:25:47,550
Just carry on as usual.

762
00:25:49,750 --> 00:25:50,860
I need a spatula.

763
00:25:51,180 --> 00:25:51,910
(Photo prop)

764
00:25:51,910 --> 00:25:52,540
Like this?

765
00:25:52,540 --> 00:25:53,180
Does this work?

766
00:25:53,590 --> 00:25:55,030
Then I'll grab a yellow pot.

767
00:25:56,860 --> 00:25:58,460
(Stiff)

768
00:25:59,110 --> 00:26:00,340
(Moves closer)
Just act a little more natural.

769
00:26:00,550 --> 00:26:02,070
Both of you, just relax.

770
00:26:02,590 --> 00:26:03,790
Come on, be natural.

771
00:26:04,460 --> 00:26:05,220
I'll be natural.

772
00:26:05,820 --> 00:26:07,140
One,

773
00:26:07,140 --> 00:26:08,220
two,

774
00:26:08,220 --> 00:26:08,780
three.

775
00:26:10,830 --> 00:26:12,070
I'll take one for you guys.

776
00:26:12,510 --> 00:26:13,430
Where do you want to take it?

777
00:26:13,620 --> 00:26:14,300
Here.

778
00:26:15,100 --> 00:26:15,980
(Looks)

779
00:26:16,220 --> 00:26:18,420
See which angle looks better for me.

780
00:26:18,620 --> 00:26:19,420
(Looks carefully)

781
00:26:19,790 --> 00:26:20,420
You two,

782
00:26:20,420 --> 00:26:21,660
(Moves closer)
move a little closer.

783
00:26:22,020 --> 00:26:23,100
A little closer.

784
00:26:23,100 --> 00:26:23,820
Is this okay?

785
00:26:23,820 --> 00:26:24,820
Yeah.

786
00:26:24,820 --> 00:26:25,430
Here we go.

787
00:26:26,420 --> 00:26:27,380
One,

788
00:26:27,380 --> 00:26:28,420
(Laughs)
two,

789
00:26:28,420 --> 00:26:29,060
three.

790
00:26:31,110 --> 00:26:31,710
Looks good.

791
00:26:31,710 --> 00:26:32,710
I was secretly smiling.

792
00:26:32,830 --> 00:26:33,430
You were?

793
00:26:33,430 --> 00:26:34,380
(Looks)
Yeah, I was.

794
00:26:34,380 --> 00:26:34,740
Yeah.

795
00:26:35,110 --> 00:26:36,070
He said he was secretly smiling.

796
00:26:38,190 --> 00:26:39,710
These two photos look pretty similar.

797
00:26:40,220 --> 00:26:40,900
But...

798
00:26:41,110 --> 00:26:42,510
this one has a pot,
and this one doesn't.

799
00:26:43,510 --> 00:26:46,390
Later, we can take another one
with a pot or something.

800
00:26:47,060 --> 00:26:52,020
(Behind-the-Scenes 21)

801
00:26:52,060 --> 00:26:54,020
(Behind-the-Scenes)

802
00:26:54,020 --> 00:26:55,510
Isn't anyone hungry?

803
00:26:56,140 --> 00:26:56,740
(Hears it)

804
00:26:59,150 --> 00:26:59,990
(Bringing food)
We'll sit here.

805
00:27:00,390 --> 00:27:01,510
But it's all snacks over here.

806
00:27:02,070 --> 00:27:02,780
Then let's sit there.

807
00:27:02,780 --> 00:27:03,270
Over there.

808
00:27:03,660 --> 00:27:05,430
(Walks over)
Is this amount of food okay?

809
00:27:09,230 --> 00:27:10,030
Which bowl?

810
00:27:10,030 --> 00:27:10,700
(Asking)

811
00:27:13,190 --> 00:27:14,190
I can combine yours if you want.

812
00:27:14,190 --> 00:27:14,980
A bigger one.

813
00:27:14,980 --> 00:27:15,740
(Transfers food)
No need.

814
00:27:16,100 --> 00:27:16,580
No need.

815
00:27:18,030 --> 00:27:19,820
You mean a bigger bowl?

816
00:27:19,820 --> 00:27:20,750
A bigger bowl.

817
00:27:22,030 --> 00:27:22,740
Sure.

818
00:27:22,740 --> 00:27:23,540
There, it's separated again.

819
00:27:25,670 --> 00:27:26,670
You're only eating this much?

820
00:27:27,590 --> 00:27:28,950
Here, I'll put this over here for you.

821
00:27:29,750 --> 00:27:30,870
That's barely anything.

822
00:27:32,230 --> 00:27:33,590
Are you trying to fatten me up?

823
00:27:33,910 --> 00:27:35,420
No, I just feel like
you need to eat more.

824
00:27:35,420 --> 00:27:36,180
You're too skinny.

825
00:27:36,180 --> 00:27:36,950
I'm not.

826
00:27:37,260 --> 00:27:38,590
I'll go get a blanket.

827
00:27:44,380 --> 00:27:45,180
It's cold.

828
00:27:46,990 --> 00:27:48,140
Chef, you sit down first.

829
00:27:48,140 --> 00:27:49,100
(Looks)

830
00:27:49,150 --> 00:27:50,030
No one's sitting.

831
00:27:51,700 --> 00:27:52,740
Then I'll sit first.

832
00:27:53,020 --> 00:27:53,860
(Laughs)

833
00:27:53,860 --> 00:27:54,750
That doesn't seem right either.

834
00:27:55,020 --> 00:27:55,820
Right?

835
00:27:58,870 --> 00:28:00,340
That smile of yours says a lot.

836
00:28:02,820 --> 00:28:07,780
(Behind-the-Scenes 22)

837
00:28:07,820 --> 00:28:11,700
(Wu Xingying & Sun Bohan return to the house)

838
00:28:11,740 --> 00:28:12,580
(Notices them)

839
00:28:13,120 --> 00:28:16,200
Hello.

840
00:28:16,270 --> 00:28:17,190
(Laughs)
Hello.

841
00:28:17,190 --> 00:28:19,350
Your smile
is practically reaching your ears.

842
00:28:19,350 --> 00:28:20,300
What have you been up to?

843
00:28:20,710 --> 00:28:22,110
We went on a city date.

844
00:28:23,150 --> 00:28:24,430
How does everyone know?

845
00:28:24,460 --> 00:28:25,460
(Laughs)

846
00:28:26,510 --> 00:28:28,070
They're all upstairs.

847
00:28:28,550 --> 00:28:29,820
They're actually all upstairs.

848
00:28:29,820 --> 00:28:30,340
Yeah.

849
00:28:31,590 --> 00:28:32,110
So many people.

850
00:28:32,590 --> 00:28:33,030
Hello, everyone.

851
00:28:33,030 --> 00:28:34,230
Why are you all upstairs?

852
00:28:34,620 --> 00:28:35,180
Yeah.

853
00:28:36,110 --> 00:28:36,980
I'm going to put my bag away.

854
00:28:36,980 --> 00:28:38,260
Okay.

855
00:28:38,550 --> 00:28:40,070
You two look so beautiful
and handsome today.

856
00:28:41,950 --> 00:28:43,260
Have you seen Si?

857
00:28:43,670 --> 00:28:45,470
She's probably on the boat.

858
00:28:45,470 --> 00:28:46,310
On the river.

859
00:28:46,430 --> 00:28:47,870
(Joking)
Go on. Go find her in the river.

860
00:28:50,070 --> 00:28:51,190
I'll go check on her.

861
00:28:54,540 --> 00:28:55,540
(Finds Si)

862
00:28:56,350 --> 00:28:58,110
This feels so nice.

863
00:28:59,380 --> 00:29:00,100
(Laughs)

864
00:29:03,110 --> 00:29:03,990
Hello.

865
00:29:04,750 --> 00:29:05,550
Hello.

866
00:29:06,390 --> 00:29:07,630
When did you get back?

867
00:29:07,630 --> 00:29:08,870
I just got back.

868
00:29:08,870 --> 00:29:09,990
Is boating tiring?

869
00:29:10,830 --> 00:29:12,030
Not really. Not too tiring.

870
00:29:12,030 --> 00:29:12,990
He says it isn't that bad.

871
00:29:15,510 --> 00:29:16,830
We'll come up later.

872
00:29:17,470 --> 00:29:18,110
No rush.

873
00:29:18,110 --> 00:29:18,980
You guys keep going.

874
00:29:18,980 --> 00:29:20,030
Carry on.

875
00:29:22,940 --> 00:29:27,900
(Behind-the-Scenes 23)

876
00:29:27,940 --> 00:29:29,820
(Behind-the-Scenes)

877
00:29:29,820 --> 00:29:30,740
(Joking)
Technically,

878
00:29:31,260 --> 00:29:32,700
we should be having a "feast" tonight.

879
00:29:34,670 --> 00:29:36,310
Isn't this the "feast" you made?

880
00:29:36,550 --> 00:29:37,910
We'll eat something better tomorrow.

881
00:29:38,950 --> 00:29:40,470
Better than that banquet.

882
00:29:43,790 --> 00:29:44,590
I'm going to get some water.

883
00:29:45,540 --> 00:29:46,180
(Looks)

884
00:29:48,670 --> 00:29:49,230
Actually,

885
00:29:49,230 --> 00:29:50,430
when I first met Yu Yang,

886
00:29:51,910 --> 00:29:53,470
I thought he looked a lot
like Bai Jingting.

887
00:29:57,390 --> 00:29:59,910
Actually, I also have a...

888
00:30:00,070 --> 00:30:01,020
(Instantly Plays Along)
"Twin brother".

889
00:30:01,270 --> 00:30:02,070
That's right.

890
00:30:02,070 --> 00:30:02,700
(Joking)

891
00:30:04,150 --> 00:30:05,510
(Turns Around)
He has a "twin brother" too.

892
00:30:06,270 --> 00:30:07,070
Seriously.

893
00:30:07,140 --> 00:30:08,710
He said he looks like Bai Jingting.

894
00:30:13,230 --> 00:30:14,750
So do you guys have any siblings?

895
00:30:15,790 --> 00:30:16,670
I'm an only child.

896
00:30:18,270 --> 00:30:19,310
Neither of us does.

897
00:30:19,380 --> 00:30:19,940
(Nods)

898
00:30:20,190 --> 00:30:21,300
I have an older brother
and an older sister.

899
00:30:22,510 --> 00:30:23,470
Both an older brother and sister?

900
00:30:23,470 --> 00:30:24,150
Yeah.

901
00:30:24,390 --> 00:30:25,670
That sounds really nice.

902
00:30:26,150 --> 00:30:26,750
So lucky.

903
00:30:30,430 --> 00:30:31,910
So how was boating yesterday?

904
00:30:33,190 --> 00:30:34,220
Pretty peaceful.

905
00:30:36,550 --> 00:30:38,940
(Curious)
Was it a long ride?

906
00:30:39,550 --> 00:30:40,630
(Listening)
How far can you go?

907
00:30:41,110 --> 00:30:43,430
You can row all the way to the area
below the stargazing room.

908
00:30:44,190 --> 00:30:45,830
But how should I put it?

909
00:30:45,830 --> 00:30:46,550
It's actually pretty fun.

910
00:30:52,590 --> 00:30:53,510
Are you guys going now?

911
00:30:53,510 --> 00:30:54,100
It's worth trying.

912
00:30:54,100 --> 00:30:55,390
But I don't think
you should stay out too late.

913
00:30:56,180 --> 00:30:56,860
(Looks over)

914
00:30:57,310 --> 00:30:58,670
I'll give you my jacket.

915
00:31:05,220 --> 00:31:07,060
=Heart Signal (China Version) S9=

916
00:31:07,060 --> 00:31:08,580
(SVIP updates every Mon & Tue at noon)

917
00:31:08,580 --> 00:31:09,980
(VIP updates every Tue & Wed at noon,
one week early)
